      "writtenOn": "2026-07-15T12:11:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These fill-ring buffers are still kernel-owned: the socket and XDP program remain active, and the producer/consumer values are only a snapshot. The kernel can consume an address after we return its buffer to VPP, potentially writing into a buffer that has already been reused. Could we first quiesce/detach the kernel path, then drain RX/partial-chain state and reclaim the remaining fill entries?",
      "revId": "ec6a3966b8ab4eb8a902b9ba53a0b8a908e6c1e5",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "01afcfef_6f954722",
        "filename": "src/plugins/af_xdp/device.c",
        "patchSetId": 40
      },
      "lineNbr": 307,
      "author": {
        "id": 361
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-15T12:11:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we make this failure fatal when multi-buffer mode was requested? Without BPF_F_XDP_HAS_FRAGS, the socket is still created with XDP_USE_SG, but the XDP program cannot process fragmented packets, so the interface appears successfully configured while multi-buffer traffic is dropped.",
      "revId": "ec6a3966b8ab4eb8a902b9ba53a0b8a908e6c1e5",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
