      "writtenOn": "2026-07-15T12:11:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "XDP_FLAGS_UPDATE_IF_NOEXIST is being passed as the mode argument here. Its value maps to XDP_MODE_NATIVE, so this unintentionally forces native XDP and breaks interfaces that require generic/SKB mode. Could we pass XDP_MODE_UNSPEC instead? The fourth argument only accepts libxdp XDP_ATTACH_* flags.",
      "revId": "ec6a3966b8ab4eb8a902b9ba53a0b8a908e6c1e5",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
